## Phase 2 — Play Styles & Round System

### Design: two-round structure

```
Round 1 (Tutorial Run)     Round 2+ (Challenge Run)
─────────────────────────    ─────────────────────────
Levels 1–50                  Levels 1–50 (new seeds)
Full undo (5)                Undo hidden / 0 undos
Timer off or generous        Timer on, tighter per level
Trail visual only            Trail = required route (Phase 3)
Reset always available       Reset limited or penalized
Forgiving move limit         Strict move limit enforced
```

### P2.1 Data model (`src/persistence.ts`)
```typescript
type TSavedProgress = {
  schemaVersion: 2;
  roundNumber: number;
  roundsCompleted: number;
  difficultyProfile: 'tutorial' | 'challenge';
  // ...existing fields
};
```
- Bump `PROGRESS_SCHEMA_VERSION`; migrate v1 → v2 (default `roundNumber: 1`).
- On beating level 50: set `roundsCompleted++`, offer "Start Round 2" on completion screen.

### P2.2 Difficulty profile (`src/difficulty.ts`)
```typescript
function getRoundConfig(round: number): TRoundConfig {
  if (round === 1) return { undoLimit: 5, timerEnabled: false, showUndo: true, enforceMoveLimit: false };
  return { undoLimit: 0, timerEnabled: true, showUndo: false, enforceMoveLimit: true, timerSeconds: 45 };
}
```
- `useGame` reads config from round instead of global constants.
- Round 2+: pass `showUndo={false}` to `Controls` (prop already exists).

### P2.3 Move limit enforcement ✅ (done early in Phase 1)
Move limit is enforced in `useGame.attemptMove`; Round 2 may add stricter per-level limits.

### P2.4 Round completion flow
- Replace auto `newLevel()` at L50 with completion modal: stats, "Challenge Round" CTA, "Play Again".
- `restartGame()` resets to Round 1; `startChallengeRound()` keeps seeds fresh, sets `roundNumber: 2`.

